1
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:39,879
Even if we go to hell,

2
00:01:40,319 --> 00:01:42,560
the bosses will be one level deeper.

3
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,319
With them out in front,

4
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:50,159
will that make the walk any faster?

5
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,200
Even if we don't, what choice do we have?

6
00:01:53,439 --> 00:01:54,439
You said before,

7
00:01:56,439 --> 00:01:59,319
anyone in any line of work can quit halfway,

8
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:00,959
but not us.

9
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:29,280
Hello. Where to?

10
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:32,960
All right. Just a moment.

11
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:36,560
Okay. That'll be 600 yuan.

12
00:02:46,159 --> 00:02:47,039
Hello. Where to?

13
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,280
A ticket to Guangzhou.

14
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,199
The earliest flight.

15
00:02:50,199 --> 00:02:51,319
All right. Just a moment.

16
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:58,319
Marijuana is too slow.

17
00:03:59,039 --> 00:04:01,759
Put what's under the leaves in the smokes.

18
00:04:02,039 --> 00:04:03,039
We need to speed things up.

19
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:11,280
There's marijuana in the cigarettes.

20
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:12,439
You have to smoke them.

21
00:04:12,439 --> 00:04:13,960
And I'll still turn you in all the same.

22
00:04:14,759 --> 00:04:17,240
Lin Kanshan and his backers are sharp.

23
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:18,160
If we don't do this,

24
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:19,160
we'll never fool them.

25
00:04:19,399 --> 00:04:22,000
We have to see the act through to the end.

26
00:04:22,079 --> 00:04:23,319
You have to suspect Lin Kanshan,

27
00:04:23,319 --> 00:04:25,199
and let him know you suspect him.

28
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:27,639
Then we'll turn ourselves in.

29
00:04:27,839 --> 00:04:29,439
Out of town. To Guangzhou State Security.

30
00:04:29,439 --> 00:04:30,639
Do you understand what I'm saying?

31
00:04:34,759 --> 00:04:35,399
I understand.

32
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:40,519
I'm pregnant.

33
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,000
It's true.

34
00:04:43,839 --> 00:04:45,240
They said there's no turning back for me,

35
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,240
but I want to turn back.

36
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:51,480
I want to build a life with you.

37
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:53,720
Then...

38
00:04:54,439 --> 00:04:55,800
What can I do?

39
00:04:56,439 --> 00:04:57,480
I'll do whatever you ask.

40
00:04:58,920 --> 00:04:59,759
Look at me.

41
00:05:00,639 --> 00:05:02,040
Remember every word I say.

42
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:03,920
Pack two sets of clothes,

43
00:05:04,279 --> 00:05:05,120
gray ones.

44
00:05:05,839 --> 00:05:07,759
Carry them yourself when we leave.

45
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:09,639
Bring only one bag.

46
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:12,120
Apart from your ID, passport, and cash,

47
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:13,439
don't pack anything else.

48
00:05:45,079 --> 00:05:46,319
Passenger Ms. Huang Ziyan,

49
00:05:46,319 --> 00:05:48,879
please hurry to Gate 103 for boarding.

50
00:05:52,319 --> 00:05:53,639
Passenger Ms. Huang Ziyan,

51
00:05:53,639 --> 00:05:56,560
please hurry to Gate 103 for boarding.

52
00:06:00,199 --> 00:06:01,519
Passenger Ms. Huang Ziyan,

53
00:06:01,519 --> 00:06:04,079
please hurry to Gate 103 for boarding.

54
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:07,560
Hello,

55
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,120
the number you dialed is powered off.

56
00:06:12,079 --> 00:06:13,399
Passenger Ms. Huang Ziyan,

57
00:06:13,399 --> 00:06:16,079
please hurry to Gate 103 for boarding.

58
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:17,399
There's still one more.

59
00:06:17,879 --> 00:06:19,199
Passenger Ms. Huang Ziyan,

60
00:06:19,199 --> 00:06:22,040
please hurry to Gate 103 for boarding.

61
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:45,399
I'm sorry, sir.

62
00:06:45,399 --> 00:06:47,240
I forgot to get gas yesterday.

63
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:53,000
You've been with me for 12 years, right?

64
00:06:53,439 --> 00:06:54,720
This is your first mistake like this.

65
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,360
Did something happen at home?

66
00:06:58,519 --> 00:06:59,600
An elder in the family passed away.

67
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:01,120
Just yesterday.

68
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:04,959
It's only natural.

69
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:06,040
Completely understandable.

70
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:08,399
Let's get gas first, then.

71
00:07:08,399 --> 00:07:10,319
Then drop me off at the office.

72
00:07:11,319 --> 00:07:13,040
Once we get there, take some time off

73
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:14,720
and hurry back home.

74
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:16,519
Understood. Thank you, sir.

75
00:07:53,639 --> 00:07:54,439
Municipal State Security Bureau

76
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:57,160
Spies are watching three sparrows.

77
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:58,480
You think it's just you?

78
00:07:58,639 --> 00:08:00,000
It's actually a game of chess.

79
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:01,480
They planned their moves long ago.

80
00:08:01,639 --> 00:08:02,639
Anticipating everything.

81
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,920
While Xie Xiaozhou was studying in Europe,

82
00:08:05,319 --> 00:08:06,480
he was already being coerced.

83
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:08,720
Your son is currently flying to Guangzhou.

84
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:10,120
Your wife is in danger, too.

85
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:11,879
We're not negotiating right now,

86
00:08:11,879 --> 00:08:12,920
nor are we testing the waters.

87
00:08:13,279 --> 00:08:14,560
What you need to do is save your life,

88
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:15,920
and the lives of your family.

89
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:17,519
Every minute you hesitate now

90
00:08:17,639 --> 00:08:19,680
puts Xie Xiaozhou in more danger.

91
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:21,160
Tell us everything.

92
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:22,040
The clearer, the better.

93
00:08:23,759 --> 00:08:25,079
Pan Xiaoying...

94
00:08:25,759 --> 00:08:26,560
How is that possible?

95
00:08:26,759 --> 00:08:27,480
In half an hour,

96
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:29,480
Xie Xiaozhou's flight will land.

97
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:30,639
Those hunting him are likely

98
00:08:30,639 --> 00:08:32,759
already waiting at the airport exit.

99
00:08:32,759 --> 00:08:33,320
Hurry up.

100
00:08:33,519 --> 00:08:35,159
We're racing against time with the enemy.

101
00:08:35,159 --> 00:08:36,159
You know what I mean.

102
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:47,159
Qiao Liang, Lin Kanshan...

103
00:08:47,159 --> 00:08:48,159
and...

104
00:08:49,039 --> 00:08:50,399
Xiaozhou's girlfriend.

105
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,360
Which one do you want me to start with?

106
00:09:13,519 --> 00:09:15,600
The person you despise is gone.

107
00:09:15,799 --> 00:09:16,879
And will never come back.

108
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:18,600
Remember what you're supposed to say.

109
00:09:18,879 --> 00:09:19,679
Thank you for your cooperation.

110
00:09:27,799 --> 00:09:29,440
When writing the Internal Reference,

111
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,360
all you need to do is steer things a bit.

112
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:31,440
No stealing secrets,

113
00:09:31,799 --> 00:09:32,679
no passing intelligence.

114
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:33,679
It's completely safe.

115
00:09:35,879 --> 00:09:37,519
As for the talk online

116
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:40,080
about a potential Taiwan Strait war,

117
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:41,919
including the reach of artillery fire,

118
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:45,879
questioning high-rises on our coast—

119
00:09:45,879 --> 00:09:47,600
that's throwing the baby out with the bathwater.

120
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:50,000
The economy is the economy.

121
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,600
It has its own laws of development,

122
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:53,879
which do not bend to human will.

123
00:09:53,879 --> 00:09:55,159
Just like driving a car:

124
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:57,279
whether hitting the gas or the brakes,

125
00:09:57,279 --> 00:09:58,720
it always takes time.

126
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,720
As for our provincial economic policy,

127
00:10:05,360 --> 00:10:07,399
properly framed, it benefits the nation and people,

128
00:10:07,759 --> 00:10:08,799
as well as your family and children.

129
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:28,399
Much of the data remains unclear right now,

130
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:35,240
so I cannot give specific advice or estimates.

131
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:39,639
Professor Pan, are you not feeling well?

132
00:10:42,799 --> 00:10:43,639
A bit of tightness in my chest.

133
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:46,519
Want me to open the window for some air?

134
00:11:10,639 --> 00:11:11,159
Come with me.

135
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:22,440
The number you dialed is powered off.

136
00:11:24,279 --> 00:11:25,720
I can't reach our son at all.

137
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:26,759
His phone is turned off, too.

138
00:11:26,759 --> 00:11:27,799
He ran away.

139
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:31,039
Can you find someone to trace his phone?

140
00:11:31,039 --> 00:11:32,279
See where he is right now.

141
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:35,120
I got out of the village to the capital,

142
00:11:35,279 --> 00:11:37,120
and only met you after going to college.

143
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:39,240
Step by step, I made it this far,

144
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,559
and haven't things turned out fine?

145
00:11:40,559 --> 00:11:41,720
What are you talking about?

146
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:43,600
Your mother was against our marriage then.

147
00:11:44,080 --> 00:11:46,360
Your family were all medical professors,

148
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:47,960
while me?

149
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:51,080
Only I got into college from my hometown.

150
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:52,720
Just a country bumpkin in the city.

151
00:11:52,919 --> 00:11:54,320
Our social standing didn't match at all.

152
00:11:54,799 --> 00:11:56,080
Looking back on it now,

153
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:59,279
it seems life's script was prewritten.

154
00:11:59,639 --> 00:12:00,679
Nobody can change it.

155
00:12:01,759 --> 00:12:04,200
So don't push Xiaozhou too hard.

156
00:12:04,559 --> 00:12:05,240
It's useless.

157
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:06,840
Lao Xie,

158
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:08,440
I'm not pushing him.

159
00:12:08,639 --> 00:12:10,960
He's sinking deeper and deeper in the mud.

160
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:12,080
If we don't pull him out,

161
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:13,240
he'll never get out.

162
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:14,399
It's about to go over his head!

163
00:12:14,399 --> 00:12:16,039
I'm telling you, I'll never agree to this!

164
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,279
Are you going to look for him or not?

165
00:12:17,279 --> 00:12:18,960
If you won't, I'm calling the police now!

166
00:12:19,799 --> 00:12:21,120
Fine, I'll look.

167
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:22,600
By the way,

168
00:12:24,039 --> 00:12:25,240
the fridge at home is broken.

169
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:26,960
If you head back around noon,

170
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:28,240
remember to have the management fix it.

171
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:29,440
Can't you just...

172
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:31,240
Can't you have the driver take care of it?

173
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:34,279
His parent passed away, so he took leave.

174
00:12:34,759 --> 00:12:36,480
You must remember to get the fridge fixed!

175
00:12:36,799 --> 00:12:38,440
Otherwise, the frozen meat inside...

176
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:39,639
just like last time,

177
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:41,080
it'll all spoil,

178
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:42,240
and the whole house will stink.

179
00:12:43,919 --> 00:12:44,679
I'm telling you...

180
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:45,639
All right, I got it.

181
00:12:45,639 --> 00:12:47,120
Go find our son! Hurry up and find him!

182
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:24,519
Is this Mr. Xie Xiaozhou?

183
00:13:24,759 --> 00:13:25,440
Yes, it's me.

184
00:13:25,639 --> 00:13:26,799
I'm a friend of your father's.

185
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:27,679
My name is Alan.

186
00:13:27,679 --> 00:13:28,480
When you get to Guangzhou,

187
00:13:28,759 --> 00:13:29,679
buy a new phone.

188
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:31,360
Use this SIM card.

189
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:32,519
The person who calls you

190
00:13:32,759 --> 00:13:33,840
can be trusted.

191
00:13:34,279 --> 00:13:36,720
And what's on this USB drive

192
00:13:37,159 --> 00:13:39,200
can buy you whatever freedom you want.

193
00:13:48,399 --> 00:13:49,159
You...

194
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:51,080
Go to America.

195
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:51,960
Leave right now.

196
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:53,000
Xie Xiaozhou, listen to me.

197
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,120
Listen to me.

198
00:13:54,759 --> 00:13:55,639
Just listen.

199
00:13:56,120 --> 00:13:57,559
Even if we turn ourselves in,

200
00:13:57,840 --> 00:13:58,639
we'll go to prison.

201
00:13:58,919 --> 00:13:59,720
We'll be sentenced.

202
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:01,240
If we go to America, we won't have to.

203
00:14:01,879 --> 00:14:02,440
We'll be free.

204
00:14:06,039 --> 00:14:06,440
Okay.

205
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:49,480
Ms. Huang, get in.

206
00:15:05,919 --> 00:15:07,080
On the north side of the building,

207
00:15:07,480 --> 00:15:09,039
there is a chain hotel.

208
00:15:09,519 --> 00:15:10,720
Someone will operate

209
00:15:10,879 --> 00:15:12,799
a remote cyber-intrusion device.

210
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:14,679
They can hack into

211
00:15:14,679 --> 00:15:15,840
every computer in this building.

212
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:19,200
The signal jammers you installed before—

213
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:20,879
I shut them all down.

214
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:22,720
It's a web.

215
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:25,120
A massive, airtight web.

216
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:28,519
Taiwan, China, since Xiaozhou was abroad,

217
00:15:28,759 --> 00:15:31,240
started laying it out, weaving it.

218
00:15:31,519 --> 00:15:33,120
Year after year,

219
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:34,440
coil after coil,

220
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:36,480
tightening ever closer.

221
00:15:37,639 --> 00:15:38,960
What else could I do?

222
00:15:40,039 --> 00:15:42,399
I couldn't stand by and watch this family

223
00:15:42,639 --> 00:15:43,919
be utterly ruined,

224
00:15:44,519 --> 00:15:45,200
torn apart.

225
00:15:46,279 --> 00:15:47,639
I knew very well

226
00:15:48,679 --> 00:15:50,720
that if I made a deal with the Americans,

227
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:53,879
once I crossed the line Qiao Liang drew,

228
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:57,639
it'd be a mistake with no turning back.

229
00:15:58,320 --> 00:15:59,519
I had no choice.

230
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:02,120
I had only one option back then:

231
00:16:02,919 --> 00:16:04,159
trade it away,

232
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:07,840
trade it for Xiaozhou's future path—

233
00:16:08,360 --> 00:16:13,000
a path of no return, full of regret.

234
00:16:28,399 --> 00:16:29,200
What's the situation?

235
00:16:35,879 --> 00:16:37,360
Minzhong City State Security Bureau

236
00:16:57,399 --> 00:16:59,120
Out there, everything's an unknown.

237
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:00,519
We'd be hostages,

238
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:01,919
captives.

239
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:03,240
If we stay,

240
00:17:04,240 --> 00:17:06,519
we turn ourselves in and go to prison.

241
00:17:08,279 --> 00:17:09,920
At least we can still be together,

242
00:17:11,119 --> 00:17:12,119
and we'll still be alive.

243
00:17:14,559 --> 00:17:16,799
I want our child to be able to see you.

244
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:23,079
According to reports,

245
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:25,359
an aerospace technology company chairman

246
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:27,680
and former vice mayor here, Xie Fengshi,

247
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:28,880
recently fell to his death.

248
00:18:29,319 --> 00:18:29,960
On the same day,

249
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:32,240
a major crash occurred on the ring road.

250
00:18:32,359 --> 00:18:34,160
A female passenger from Taiwan, China,

251
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:36,359
and a local male passenger in the same car

252
00:18:36,480 --> 00:18:38,960
died from severe injuries after treatment.

253
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,920
The others are receiving treatment,

254
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:43,079
and the cause is under investigation.

255
00:19:02,559 --> 00:19:03,440
You're safe now.

256
00:19:04,559 --> 00:19:05,240
What did they say?

257
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:06,160
I can't hear it clearly.

258
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:09,039
The two who knew your background have vanished.

259
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:10,160
Forever.

260
00:19:23,799 --> 00:19:25,359
So what do I need to do now?

261
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:27,519
Go back where you belong.

262
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:29,839
Run your business.

263
00:19:29,839 --> 00:19:30,960
Make your RMB.

264
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:32,119
Be the boss.

265
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:34,119
What else do you want?

266
00:19:36,759 --> 00:19:38,039
Are you listening to me?

267
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:41,440
Don't be nervous.

268
00:19:41,559 --> 00:19:44,240
Just live your life like before.

269
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:46,079
Just keep your ears open,

270
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:47,680
your eyes peeled,

271
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:48,519
and your mind clear,

272
00:19:48,519 --> 00:19:49,640
and you'll be fine.

273
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:51,160
Fine.

274
00:19:55,079 --> 00:19:56,480
Keep doing things like this,

275
00:19:57,839 --> 00:19:59,319
and you'll really go to hell.

276
00:20:05,759 --> 00:20:06,480
Step out!

277
00:20:18,079 --> 00:20:20,119
Forward, march!

278
00:20:34,319 --> 00:20:37,920
Left, right, left! Left, right, left!

279
00:20:38,559 --> 00:20:42,160
Left, right, left! Left, right, left!

280
00:20:42,359 --> 00:20:43,119
Reporting, sir!

281
00:20:43,119 --> 00:20:43,799
Step out!

282
00:20:43,799 --> 00:20:45,160
Yes, sir. My shoe came off.

283
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:45,839
Fix it.

284
00:20:45,839 --> 00:20:46,720
Yes, sir!

285
00:20:51,319 --> 00:20:51,920
Catch up!

286
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:52,519
Yes, sir!

287
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:55,680
Heard you switched cigarette brands.

288
00:20:55,759 --> 00:20:57,000
Got quite the connections.

289
00:20:57,480 --> 00:20:59,160
When did you get back from rehab?

290
00:20:59,160 --> 00:21:00,920
We're stuck doing hard labor,

291
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:03,559
while you enjoy the fan in the computer room.

292
00:21:04,200 --> 00:21:05,920
Stop pretending you can install an OS.

293
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:07,519
I know someone's looking out for you.

294
00:21:07,519 --> 00:21:08,519
What are you getting at?

295
00:21:08,759 --> 00:21:11,200
They only know you as a robber, right?

296
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:13,559
If word gets out you stole government files

297
00:21:13,559 --> 00:21:15,640
and peddled classified intel,

298
00:21:15,640 --> 00:21:17,039
wouldn't they add years to your sentence?

299
00:21:19,599 --> 00:21:20,759
Threatening me?

300
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:22,119
Go ahead and tell them!

301
00:21:23,279 --> 00:21:24,720
You know I've been a vegetarian so long

302
00:21:25,240 --> 00:21:26,279
that I'm malnourished.

303
00:21:26,279 --> 00:21:27,680
I really can't keep up physically.

304
00:21:27,920 --> 00:21:29,279
Put in a word with your guy.

305
00:21:29,720 --> 00:21:31,920
Help me switch to an easier job.

306
00:21:33,079 --> 00:21:34,000
What's the chatter back there?

307
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:34,599
Keep up!

308
00:21:34,599 --> 00:21:35,279
Yes, sir! Right away, sir!

309
00:21:38,279 --> 00:21:39,359
Can you do it?

310
00:21:39,599 --> 00:21:40,559
Depends on how you behave.

311
00:21:42,519 --> 00:21:43,400
It's a deal, then.

312
00:21:45,519 --> 00:21:47,359
Now turning to international news.

313
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:48,920
During a campaign event in South Korea,

314
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:50,160
an attack took place.

315
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:51,640
Police have launched an investigation.

316
00:21:51,640 --> 00:21:53,519
According to South Korea's Yonhap News,

317
00:21:53,720 --> 00:21:55,880
on the 20th, the main opposition leader,

318
00:21:55,880 --> 00:21:57,640
Park Geun-hye of the Grand National Party...

319
00:21:57,640 --> 00:21:59,680
Tell me, how did you guess it?

320
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:01,680
Nine out of ten gamblers lose.

321
00:22:02,400 --> 00:22:03,839
They lose because they guess.

322
00:22:03,839 --> 00:22:05,400
You have to analyze it.

323
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:07,240
Use your brain, understand?

324
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:09,640
Do you think this is real or fake?

325
00:22:09,640 --> 00:22:10,960
Half a pack of instant noodles

326
00:22:11,160 --> 00:22:12,200
and a bag of pickled mustard.

327
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:15,119
We've got time to kill anyway,

328
00:22:15,119 --> 00:22:16,559
and we're in no rush to sleep.

329
00:22:16,559 --> 00:22:19,000
When Chen Shui-bian was shot two years ago,

330
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:20,720
your deduction was spot-on.

331
00:22:20,720 --> 00:22:22,680
Why don't you analyze this one, then?

332
00:22:25,079 --> 00:22:26,039
In the upcoming

333
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:28,559
LDP election in Japan,

334
00:22:29,480 --> 00:22:30,759
who will win and who will lose?

335
00:22:31,279 --> 00:22:32,440
One cigarette each.

336
00:22:32,599 --> 00:22:33,440
Care to bet?

337
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:34,640
I'm in.

338
00:22:35,119 --> 00:22:35,599
I'm in.

339
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:37,000
I'm in.

340
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:37,400
I'm in.

341
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:37,880
I'm in.

342
00:22:39,480 --> 00:22:40,440
I'm in.

343
00:22:56,880 --> 00:22:57,640
Jinlan

344
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:23,240
We're sorry,

345
00:23:23,640 --> 00:23:26,599
the subscriber you dialed is unavailable.

346
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:28,599
Please try again later.

347
00:23:44,039 --> 00:23:44,839
What?

348
00:23:45,359 --> 00:23:46,559
Your mother had a stroke.

349
00:23:57,039 --> 00:23:58,599
A consultation is definitely a good idea.

350
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:00,640
No problem at all.

351
00:24:00,720 --> 00:24:01,799
I have no objection.

352
00:24:02,119 --> 00:24:03,039
I agree.

353
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:04,680
But the most important thing right now

354
00:24:04,680 --> 00:24:06,319
is deciding on a treatment plan.

355
00:24:06,759 --> 00:24:07,920
Right?

356
00:24:07,920 --> 00:24:09,960
Two heads are definitely better than one.

357
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:11,720
Having more experts take a look

358
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:13,640
is totally fine and necessary.

359
00:24:14,079 --> 00:24:16,319
I'll discuss it with my child when I get back.

360
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:18,759
Three questions.

361
00:24:18,759 --> 00:24:19,440
First.

362
00:24:19,799 --> 00:24:21,599
Was Mom's blood pressure stable before she fell ill?

363
00:24:21,920 --> 00:24:22,519
Second.

364
00:24:22,519 --> 00:24:24,319
Did she ever complain to you about headaches,

365
00:24:24,559 --> 00:24:26,160
or constantly having blurry vision?

366
00:24:26,359 --> 00:24:26,880
Did she?

367
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:28,319
I never heard her mention it.

368
00:24:28,680 --> 00:24:31,480
But blurry vision from old age is normal.

369
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:33,079
When she was first admitted,

370
00:24:33,079 --> 00:24:34,759
you said she fell ill at home.

371
00:24:34,759 --> 00:24:36,319
At morning rounds you said downstairs.

372
00:24:36,319 --> 00:24:37,240
Where exactly was it?

373
00:24:38,039 --> 00:24:40,240
She felt unwell going down for groceries.

374
00:24:40,240 --> 00:24:42,480
Once home, she felt awful and needed rest.

375
00:24:42,759 --> 00:24:44,200
And then she wouldn't wake up.

376
00:24:47,400 --> 00:24:47,839
Look,

377
00:24:47,839 --> 00:24:49,000
go home and get some good rest.

378
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:49,960
Don't overthink things.

379
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:51,319
Take care of yourself.

380
00:24:51,759 --> 00:24:52,960
Eat well, sleep well,

381
00:24:52,960 --> 00:24:54,000
and come relieve me tomorrow.

382
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:55,920
None of us can afford to collapse right now.

383
00:24:56,200 --> 00:24:57,559
Who'll look after things if I leave?

384
00:24:57,839 --> 00:24:59,160
Chunxiao and I will.

385
00:25:00,119 --> 00:25:00,920
I've got it covered here.

386
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:02,200
Go on, head out now.

387
00:25:02,920 --> 00:25:03,759
All right.

388
00:25:12,759 --> 00:25:14,079
I'm on my way.

389
00:25:14,079 --> 00:25:15,319
I was almost there,

390
00:25:15,319 --> 00:25:16,200
but something came up

391
00:25:16,200 --> 00:25:17,599
so I need to head back to the office.

392
00:25:17,759 --> 00:25:18,519
Gotta hang up now.

393
00:25:24,680 --> 00:25:26,599
I'm off. Let me know of any news about Mom.

394
00:25:29,440 --> 00:25:30,119
Dad.

395
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:32,200
Don't wait till tomorrow.

396
00:25:33,160 --> 00:25:34,359
Just come relieve me once you wake up.

397
00:25:35,559 --> 00:25:36,359
Okay.

398
00:26:07,960 --> 00:26:08,839
I'm so sorry.

399
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:10,599
Really, I'm sorry.

400
00:26:11,440 --> 00:26:12,599
This is the first time I've been late.

401
00:26:16,519 --> 00:26:17,799
I thought you'd already left.

402
00:26:19,680 --> 00:26:21,200
Did something happen?

403
00:26:21,720 --> 00:26:22,599
No.

404
00:26:23,039 --> 00:26:24,880
Just busy, and I misread the time.

405
00:26:28,079 --> 00:26:28,920
Lately, I...

406
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:30,119
If you're tired,

407
00:26:30,119 --> 00:26:31,640
we can sit down and rest a bit.

408
00:26:32,559 --> 00:26:33,440
It's fine.

409
00:26:34,559 --> 00:26:35,480
I'll stay with you.

410
00:27:43,880 --> 00:27:44,680
Dad.

411
00:27:47,680 --> 00:27:49,799
Is your signal bad?

412
00:27:49,799 --> 00:27:51,160
Can you hear me?

413
00:27:51,519 --> 00:27:53,240
Can you hear me talking?

414
00:27:54,079 --> 00:27:55,680
I can hear you. Can you hear me?

415
00:27:56,039 --> 00:27:57,480
I can hear you!

416
00:27:59,440 --> 00:28:00,880
Why are you up so early?

417
00:28:01,640 --> 00:28:03,119
I was worried you weren't awake yet.

418
00:28:03,119 --> 00:28:04,640
At my age,

419
00:28:04,640 --> 00:28:06,359
how could I sleep in?

420
00:28:07,279 --> 00:28:08,599
Why does your voice sound weird?

421
00:28:09,400 --> 00:28:10,519
Are you sick?

422
00:28:10,519 --> 00:28:11,880
I don't have a cold.

423
00:28:11,880 --> 00:28:14,839
That's just how you sound lying down.

424
00:28:14,839 --> 00:28:17,559
Is that volunteer of yours with you?

425
00:28:17,559 --> 00:28:19,519
What do you care if she is or not?

426
00:28:19,519 --> 00:28:20,599
You never come home anyway.

427
00:28:20,720 --> 00:28:23,000
I had that chubby girl replaced for you.

428
00:28:23,279 --> 00:28:24,079
Did they replace her?

429
00:28:24,319 --> 00:28:25,880
So you were the one who had her replaced!

430
00:28:25,880 --> 00:28:27,319
You just didn't want her replaced, right?

431
00:28:27,319 --> 00:28:29,000
You just like chubby girls, don't you?

432
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:30,440
What's wrong with chubby girls?

433
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:32,359
She's good-hearted.

434
00:28:32,759 --> 00:28:33,640
You're not around,

435
00:28:33,880 --> 00:28:35,680
so I rely on her to take care of me.

436
00:28:35,920 --> 00:28:37,680
She even introduced fellow believers to me.

437
00:28:37,880 --> 00:28:38,839
All right, all right.

438
00:28:38,839 --> 00:28:39,880
As long as you like her.

439
00:28:39,880 --> 00:28:41,079
No need to report it to me.

440
00:28:41,319 --> 00:28:42,839
So what does your religion preach?

441
00:28:43,160 --> 00:28:45,079
It preaches conscience and faith.

442
00:28:45,480 --> 00:28:47,000
Better than certain people

443
00:28:47,200 --> 00:28:48,200
who only care about money.

444
00:28:48,680 --> 00:28:50,200
Last time, I heard someone say

445
00:28:50,200 --> 00:28:52,440
that people go to heaven after they die,

446
00:28:52,759 --> 00:28:54,319
because the mortal world is hell.

447
00:28:54,799 --> 00:28:55,640
Is that really a thing?

448
00:28:55,640 --> 00:28:57,039
What are you talking about?

449
00:28:57,039 --> 00:28:58,400
Do rituals for the dead actually work?

450
00:28:58,799 --> 00:29:00,240
Are you drunk?

451
00:29:00,240 --> 00:29:01,599
I'm not drunk.

452
00:29:01,599 --> 00:29:02,960
I'm completely sober.

453
00:29:02,960 --> 00:29:04,160
I'm just asking for your insight.

454
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:06,759
You're either drunk or out of your mind.

455
00:29:07,200 --> 00:29:08,319
That chubby girl...

456
00:29:08,319 --> 00:29:10,000
complained that you sneak pastries.

457
00:29:10,480 --> 00:29:11,440
Who sneaked anything?

458
00:29:11,440 --> 00:29:12,960
I just had a little taste.

459
00:29:12,960 --> 00:29:14,160
See, the moment I bring this up,

460
00:29:14,160 --> 00:29:15,240
you start making excuses.

461
00:29:15,240 --> 00:29:17,160
If you want to eat pastries, eat them,

462
00:29:17,160 --> 00:29:18,960
just remember to check your blood sugar.

463
00:29:18,960 --> 00:29:20,039
Stop acting like a thief.

464
00:29:20,039 --> 00:29:20,519
Just be open about it.

465
00:29:20,519 --> 00:29:21,759
If that's all, I'm hanging up.

466
00:29:21,759 --> 00:29:22,240
Fine, fine.

467
00:29:22,240 --> 00:29:23,680
Bring this up, and you want to hang up.

468
00:29:24,640 --> 00:29:25,559
Cut down on sweets.

469
00:29:29,519 --> 00:29:30,400
Got a cold...

470
00:29:31,960 --> 00:29:34,000
A lot piled up while you were gone.

471
00:29:34,119 --> 00:29:35,200
The documents needing your signature

472
00:29:35,200 --> 00:29:37,039
are already on your desk.

473
00:29:37,039 --> 00:29:38,920
There are two groups you must meet.

474
00:29:38,920 --> 00:29:40,519
Either two separate meetings at noon,

475
00:29:40,519 --> 00:29:41,440
or one in the evening

476
00:29:41,440 --> 00:29:42,279
and one at noon.

477
00:29:42,279 --> 00:29:43,240
Depending on how you want to schedule it.

478
00:29:45,119 --> 00:29:46,319
I'm not feeling well.

479
00:29:46,759 --> 00:29:47,920
Might have caught a cold.

480
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:49,000
I'm heading home to rest first.

481
00:29:49,200 --> 00:29:50,359
Handle the visitors for me.

482
00:29:50,599 --> 00:29:51,799
As for the contracts to sign,

483
00:29:51,799 --> 00:29:53,559
my name stamp is in the drawer.

484
00:29:53,559 --> 00:29:54,759
Just take care of them yourself.

485
00:29:55,480 --> 00:29:56,440
Take care of yourself.

486
00:30:54,559 --> 00:30:55,359
Are you done?

487
00:30:55,359 --> 00:30:56,480
If you're done, listen to me.

488
00:30:56,480 --> 00:30:57,599
Please don't interrupt me.

489
00:30:58,039 --> 00:31:00,200
Who concluded that my mom had a relapse?

490
00:31:00,200 --> 00:31:01,880
Was it you, the doctor, or who?

491
00:31:01,880 --> 00:31:03,279
Just tell me who it was.

492
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:04,279
Dad, stop giving me

493
00:31:04,279 --> 00:31:06,119
your subjective assumptions.

494
00:31:06,119 --> 00:31:07,400
I want to hear what the doctor says.

495
00:31:07,400 --> 00:31:08,440
Are you a doctor?

496
00:31:08,799 --> 00:31:10,119
If you still don't understand what I mean,

497
00:31:10,119 --> 00:31:11,440
I'll come to the hospital right now.

498
00:31:11,880 --> 00:31:13,559
Stop making blind assumptions.

499
00:31:13,559 --> 00:31:15,240
I want to hear from the doctor.

500
00:31:15,240 --> 00:31:16,440
Go ask the nurse.

501
00:31:16,519 --> 00:31:18,039
Call me back once you've found out.

502
00:31:19,680 --> 00:31:21,880
I was cut off mid-call earlier.

503
00:31:22,400 --> 00:31:23,440
My phone died.

504
00:31:23,680 --> 00:31:24,680
Is something wrong?

505
00:31:26,119 --> 00:31:27,039
It's fine now.

506
00:31:29,319 --> 00:31:30,880
How's your mom doing?

507
00:31:31,279 --> 00:31:32,160
She's stable for now.

508
00:31:32,160 --> 00:31:33,279
She still needs to stay for observation.

509
00:31:36,119 --> 00:31:37,799
My stomach's been bothering me lately.

510
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:39,279
Is there any porridge at home?

511
00:32:28,359 --> 00:32:29,160
Jinlan.

512
00:32:29,559 --> 00:32:31,960
How did I end up sleeping in the bathroom all night?

513
00:32:33,240 --> 00:32:34,720
What time did I get back last night?

514
00:32:37,279 --> 00:32:38,440
There's porridge in the fridge.

515
00:32:38,440 --> 00:32:39,400
Leftovers from two days ago.

516
00:32:39,400 --> 00:32:40,480
See if it's still good.

517
00:32:42,680 --> 00:32:44,400
Why has your phone been turned off?

518
00:32:45,079 --> 00:32:45,680
What happened?

519
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:48,279
Did the battery died?

520
00:32:50,759 --> 00:32:51,559
As long as you're okay.

521
00:32:52,680 --> 00:32:53,680
You called me in the middle of the night.

522
00:32:53,680 --> 00:32:54,640
I missed it.

523
00:32:54,799 --> 00:32:55,880
I was worried something had happened to you.

524
00:33:04,160 --> 00:33:05,559
Honestly, I didn't want to drink either.

525
00:33:06,319 --> 00:33:07,440
But I had no choice.

526
00:33:07,599 --> 00:33:08,680
Couldn't avoid it.

527
00:33:08,839 --> 00:33:09,759
Only now do I realize

528
00:33:09,759 --> 00:33:11,519
how hard it is to run a business alone.

529
00:33:15,119 --> 00:33:16,119
I know.

530
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:18,079
Things won't be affected on my end.

531
00:33:18,240 --> 00:33:19,920
We'll still stick to the agreed time.

532
00:33:20,440 --> 00:33:21,359
In the fall, right?

533
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:22,519
Why don't you talk to her

534
00:33:22,519 --> 00:33:24,160
and hold off on contact for a few days?

535
00:33:24,480 --> 00:33:26,079
Make sure you get some rest lately too.

536
00:33:29,720 --> 00:33:31,519
If you really care, stop drinking.

537
00:33:33,839 --> 00:33:35,640
I know you're busy over there,

538
00:33:35,640 --> 00:33:37,599
but I have plenty of headaches here too.

539
00:33:38,160 --> 00:33:38,680
Last night,

540
00:33:38,680 --> 00:33:40,000
you just watched me sleep in the bathroom,

541
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:40,799
the entire night.

542
00:33:41,119 --> 00:33:41,519
I mean,

543
00:33:41,519 --> 00:33:43,440
even if you brought home a stray cat or dog,

544
00:33:43,440 --> 00:33:44,759
you wouldn't just leave it all by itself in...

545
00:33:56,319 --> 00:33:57,079
One more time! One more time!

546
00:33:57,079 --> 00:33:57,680
Nice shot!

547
00:33:59,160 --> 00:33:59,759
Nice shot!

548
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:03,200
Thanks, man.

549
00:34:03,880 --> 00:34:05,440
Finally, a break from the sewing machines.

550
00:34:05,440 --> 00:34:07,480
You walk the fastest out here in the yard.

551
00:34:07,680 --> 00:34:08,480
Got so much strength in your legs.

552
00:34:08,480 --> 00:34:10,119
Obviously, you're not working hard enough.

553
00:34:10,119 --> 00:34:11,159
Aren't you supposed to be so smart?

554
00:34:11,159 --> 00:34:12,320
Why didn't you just fake it?

555
00:34:12,320 --> 00:34:15,079
Smarts only count if you can cash them in.

556
00:34:15,079 --> 00:34:17,880
Could you connect me with your friend?

557
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:19,119
Once we get out of here,

558
00:34:19,679 --> 00:34:20,679
we can do some business together.

559
00:34:21,119 --> 00:34:22,000
What kind of business?

560
00:34:25,599 --> 00:34:27,719
Next, turning to international news.

561
00:34:28,519 --> 00:34:31,360
Japan's LDP election results are in.

562
00:34:31,360 --> 00:34:33,199
Shinzo Abe won by a landslide,

563
00:34:33,360 --> 00:34:36,039
taking first place with 464 votes.

564
00:34:36,039 --> 00:34:38,280
Taro Aso received 136 votes,

565
00:34:38,280 --> 00:34:39,320
coming in second.

566
00:34:40,119 --> 00:34:41,039
I'm blown away.

567
00:34:41,920 --> 00:34:44,760
To me, you're the God of Gamblers.

568
00:34:47,159 --> 00:34:48,119
Stay away from me.

569
00:34:48,239 --> 00:34:49,320
Don't let the guards see us.

570
00:34:49,400 --> 00:34:50,079
Impressive.

571
00:34:50,440 --> 00:34:52,079
I'm completely in awe of you.

572
00:35:19,599 --> 00:35:20,480
I'll pay for the lesson.

573
00:35:27,800 --> 00:35:28,559
Tell me.

574
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:30,719
You have no access to information here,

575
00:35:31,440 --> 00:35:33,320
so how did you pull it off?

576
00:35:33,800 --> 00:35:35,440
Could it be possible

577
00:35:35,440 --> 00:35:38,760
that long posing as military security,

578
00:35:39,559 --> 00:35:40,760
your every gesture,

579
00:35:40,760 --> 00:35:42,000
every word and deed,

580
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:43,880
and even your subconscious—

581
00:35:44,679 --> 00:35:47,360
your grasp of this imagined profession

582
00:35:47,360 --> 00:35:49,000
has seeped into your very bones?

583
00:35:49,320 --> 00:35:50,719
That's why you have clear ideas,

584
00:35:51,159 --> 00:35:52,159
you have logic,

585
00:35:53,119 --> 00:35:54,519
and that's why you're professional.

586
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:02,519
Let me put it this way.

587
00:36:03,519 --> 00:36:06,079
Anyone who wins money at the gambling table

588
00:36:06,519 --> 00:36:07,719
is a professional.

589
00:36:08,239 --> 00:36:09,079
Then tell me,

590
00:36:09,920 --> 00:36:13,719
when will mainland and Taiwan, China reunite?

591
00:36:20,480 --> 00:36:25,519
When some things happen is uncertain,

592
00:36:27,320 --> 00:36:28,840
but they are bound to happen.

593
00:36:29,760 --> 00:36:32,159
If someone gives you a specific date,

594
00:36:33,920 --> 00:36:35,360
he's definitely a fraud.

595
00:36:54,360 --> 00:36:55,920
One box is from Europe,

596
00:36:55,920 --> 00:36:57,119
and one is from the US.

597
00:36:57,920 --> 00:36:59,280
A stroke is serious business.

598
00:36:59,280 --> 00:36:59,960
Give them a try first.

599
00:36:59,960 --> 00:37:00,960
Desperate times call for desperate measures.

600
00:37:04,039 --> 00:37:04,840
Thanks.

601
00:37:05,960 --> 00:37:07,880
I had a fortune teller do a reading.

602
00:37:07,880 --> 00:37:09,880
Some things shouldn't be heard by Jinlan.

603
00:37:10,199 --> 00:37:11,000
Let's talk somewhere else.

604
00:37:15,400 --> 00:37:16,280
Thank you, truly.

605
00:37:18,800 --> 00:37:19,480
No more, I can't drink anymore.

606
00:37:19,480 --> 00:37:21,320
Had too much yesterday, almost got wasted.

607
00:37:21,840 --> 00:37:23,039
Hair of the dog, it'll clear your head!

608
00:37:23,559 --> 00:37:24,480
Come on, drink up.

609
00:37:24,760 --> 00:37:27,719
Remember last time when you and Brother Qi forced drinks on me?

610
00:37:28,320 --> 00:37:29,679
You even made me drink plum wine.

611
00:37:29,679 --> 00:37:31,840
When I got home, I threw up everything

612
00:37:31,840 --> 00:37:32,840
I'd had since primary school.

613
00:37:32,840 --> 00:37:34,360
The next day, you wanted me to keep drinking.

614
00:37:34,519 --> 00:37:35,480
And you made me drink baijiu!

615
00:37:35,599 --> 00:37:37,599
I thought you were trying to kill me.

616
00:37:38,280 --> 00:37:40,840
Sometimes a little hair of the dog helps.

617
00:37:41,159 --> 00:37:42,679
True brothers push you to drink.

618
00:37:49,440 --> 00:37:50,639
About your mother-in-law...

619
00:37:50,960 --> 00:37:52,119
The situation isn't good.

620
00:37:52,880 --> 00:37:54,199
That's why we need to find solutions.

621
00:37:54,519 --> 00:37:56,480
At least we won't have regrets if we try.

622
00:38:00,360 --> 00:38:03,599
I burned incense for you at Mount Dagu,

623
00:38:04,159 --> 00:38:05,119
and had a Taoist ritual performed.

624
00:38:05,400 --> 00:38:06,400
Tonight,

625
00:38:06,400 --> 00:38:07,960
just get a good night's sleep.

626
00:38:07,960 --> 00:38:08,920
Stop arguing.

627
00:38:08,920 --> 00:38:10,719
When you smash things, I can't sleep either.

628
00:38:12,760 --> 00:38:13,639
It's all in the drink.

629
00:38:20,239 --> 00:38:21,639
Marriage is all about give and take.

630
00:38:21,679 --> 00:38:22,599
You give in today,

631
00:38:22,599 --> 00:38:23,800
and I'll give in tomorrow.

632
00:38:24,079 --> 00:38:25,360
Once that sense of distance

633
00:38:25,559 --> 00:38:27,159
is broken, things turn sour.

634
00:38:27,400 --> 00:38:28,199
It feels suffocating.

635
00:38:28,800 --> 00:38:30,239
Look how great I have it.

636
00:38:30,440 --> 00:38:31,960
Just date, never marry.

637
00:38:32,320 --> 00:38:33,960
Keeping some distance is wonderful.

638
00:38:34,239 --> 00:38:36,159
Finding the right balance is the hardest.

639
00:38:36,280 --> 00:38:38,400
Sometimes, you take a step forward,

640
00:38:38,880 --> 00:38:40,119
and one step too far causes a fight.

641
00:38:40,280 --> 00:38:41,800
Then you take a step back,

642
00:38:41,800 --> 00:38:44,119
and she thinks you're uncaring and cold.

643
00:38:44,280 --> 00:38:45,800
Medical treatments are just like that.

644
00:38:46,239 --> 00:38:47,719
Everyone has different opinions.

645
00:38:47,719 --> 00:38:49,199
I'm just a son-in-law,

646
00:38:49,199 --> 00:38:50,320
not her actual son.

647
00:38:50,320 --> 00:38:51,599
The more I say, the more I mess up.

648
00:38:51,599 --> 00:38:52,480
Chinese medicine or Western medicine?

649
00:38:52,480 --> 00:38:53,880
No matter what I say, it's always wrong.

650
00:38:55,559 --> 00:38:57,480
You sure have a lot to say today.

651
00:38:57,480 --> 00:38:58,239
That's rare for you.

652
00:38:58,480 --> 00:39:01,079
Midlife brings endless troubles.

653
00:39:01,840 --> 00:39:02,480
So you talk more.

654
00:39:04,559 --> 00:39:06,760
Some troubles are just fated.

655
00:39:07,400 --> 00:39:09,239
Remember when we got our fortune told?

656
00:39:09,239 --> 00:39:10,079
The three of us.

657
00:39:10,639 --> 00:39:11,599
What did yours say?

658
00:39:13,320 --> 00:39:15,440
"Eight thousand li of clouds and moon."

659
00:39:16,679 --> 00:39:17,679
Fated to toil away.

660
00:39:17,679 --> 00:39:18,639
Look at me now.

661
00:39:19,599 --> 00:39:20,800
I'm running myself ragged.

662
00:39:20,800 --> 00:39:21,920
That was Yue Fei!

663
00:39:22,239 --> 00:39:23,559
A great national hero.

664
00:39:23,639 --> 00:39:25,400
It's only natural to toil like him.

665
00:39:25,639 --> 00:39:27,159
My mom always told me

666
00:39:27,239 --> 00:39:30,320
we're born to suffer in life.

667
00:39:30,880 --> 00:39:31,760
Look at my mother-in-law.

668
00:39:32,199 --> 00:39:33,519
She toiled her whole life,

669
00:39:33,599 --> 00:39:34,920
and now she's bedridden.

670
00:39:35,320 --> 00:39:36,719
Barely two days in bed,

671
00:39:36,920 --> 00:39:38,320
and the doctor says it could be fatal.

672
00:39:38,599 --> 00:39:40,440
Not because of the issue in her brain,

673
00:39:41,119 --> 00:39:41,840
but her legs.

674
00:39:42,079 --> 00:39:43,760
They're worried about vein thrombosis.

675
00:39:43,960 --> 00:39:45,880
If a clot travels up to her lungs,

676
00:39:45,880 --> 00:39:46,760
she's gone.

677
00:39:47,239 --> 00:39:48,440
She worked hard all her life,

678
00:39:49,000 --> 00:39:51,119
and now even resting is a curse.

679
00:39:52,000 --> 00:39:52,960
What do they call it?

680
00:39:53,760 --> 00:39:55,239
"Toiling away day in, day out,

681
00:39:55,559 --> 00:39:57,599
never a moment's peace."

682
00:40:05,320 --> 00:40:06,039
What about you?

683
00:40:06,519 --> 00:40:08,000
What character did you pick back then?

684
00:40:09,119 --> 00:40:10,719
Let me think, what was it again?

685
00:40:12,239 --> 00:40:14,840
"Water flowing down shoals has no intent,"

686
00:40:15,159 --> 00:40:17,840
and drifting white clouds have no design."

687
00:40:18,360 --> 00:40:20,079
Later, I went and asked Wen Zongshu

688
00:40:20,079 --> 00:40:21,679
what it actually meant.

689
00:40:21,920 --> 00:40:22,920
He told me

690
00:40:23,159 --> 00:40:23,960
that in this world,

691
00:40:23,960 --> 00:40:26,599
so much happens by pure chance,

692
00:40:27,480 --> 00:40:28,599
ordained by fate,

693
00:40:28,719 --> 00:40:30,039
and you can't change any of it.

694
00:40:30,039 --> 00:40:30,960
That's why I follow Daoism.

695
00:40:31,239 --> 00:40:32,719
My fate is in my own hands, not heaven's.

696
00:40:32,960 --> 00:40:34,079
We're businessmen.

697
00:40:34,559 --> 00:40:35,800
You have no control over anything.

698
00:40:36,199 --> 00:40:37,760
Crossing the sea to the mainland,

699
00:40:37,760 --> 00:40:39,239
I don't even know what I'm rambling about.

700
00:40:44,239 --> 00:40:45,719
The first time I met Wen Zongshu,

701
00:40:46,159 --> 00:40:47,400
he was flying high,

702
00:40:47,400 --> 00:40:49,639
lecturing all the hostesses in the private room,

703
00:40:50,599 --> 00:40:51,400
telling them

704
00:40:51,760 --> 00:40:54,320
so many things in life are predestined.

705
00:40:54,519 --> 00:40:56,000
Like who marries whom,

706
00:40:56,519 --> 00:40:57,440
or who takes whom as a wife,

707
00:40:57,840 --> 00:40:59,639
or how high an official you become.

708
00:40:59,639 --> 00:41:01,000
All of it is predetermined,

709
00:41:01,199 --> 00:41:02,000
impossible to change.

710
00:41:02,679 --> 00:41:03,760
Yet some things,

711
00:41:03,960 --> 00:41:05,239
you actually can change.

712
00:41:05,719 --> 00:41:07,480
Spouse, wealth, children, rank, and life.

713
00:41:07,960 --> 00:41:09,000
Except for spouse and rank,

714
00:41:09,000 --> 00:41:10,280
the other three can be altered.

715
00:41:10,920 --> 00:41:11,719
How do you change them?

716
00:41:12,920 --> 00:41:13,719
Do more good deeds.

717
00:41:14,760 --> 00:41:16,280
The more good deeds you do,

718
00:41:16,280 --> 00:41:19,280
the more your life and wealth will expand.

719
00:41:24,639 --> 00:41:26,480
I only date and never lead them on to marry.

720
00:41:26,480 --> 00:41:28,000
It's easier on the girls that way, right?

721
00:41:28,000 --> 00:41:29,159
Does that count as doing good deeds?

722
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:34,440
Don't open it. No more.

723
00:41:34,440 --> 00:41:35,760
Come on, just one more bottle.

724
00:41:35,760 --> 00:41:38,079
"After this cup, there are three more!"

725
00:41:59,960 --> 00:42:01,039
As for this medicine,

726
00:42:01,039 --> 00:42:02,679
take two pills three times a day.

727
00:42:03,079 --> 00:42:04,199
How are the clinical results?

728
00:42:04,199 --> 00:42:05,320
The clinical results are excellent.

729
00:42:05,320 --> 00:42:05,880
Really?

730
00:42:06,320 --> 00:42:08,159
If they're good, then we can give it a try, right?

731
00:42:08,159 --> 00:42:10,239
Chunxiao, talk some sense into her too.

732
00:42:10,239 --> 00:42:11,719
We can't do surgery.

733
00:42:11,719 --> 00:42:13,480
The risk is just too high.

734
00:42:13,960 --> 00:42:15,000
Dad, have you eaten?

735
00:42:15,440 --> 00:42:16,199
Can't you see

736
00:42:16,199 --> 00:42:17,840
we're discussing her treatment?

737
00:42:17,840 --> 00:42:19,239
How could I eat at a time like this?

738
00:42:19,239 --> 00:42:20,599
If you've eaten, just say so.

739
00:42:20,599 --> 00:42:21,880
If not, go eat over there.

740
00:42:21,880 --> 00:42:22,840
Stop shouting.

741
00:42:23,079 --> 00:42:24,840
If Mom were awake, you'd annoy her too.

742
00:42:25,039 --> 00:42:26,159
Go back and get some rest.

743
00:42:26,159 --> 00:42:27,159
As for the treatment plan,

744
00:42:27,159 --> 00:42:28,239
we can decide on it.

745
00:42:29,480 --> 00:42:30,320
What's that supposed to mean?

746
00:42:30,679 --> 00:42:31,679
It means being scientific.

747
00:42:31,679 --> 00:42:32,719
It means being professional.

748
00:42:32,840 --> 00:42:34,320
Conservative treatment is too risky.

749
00:42:34,320 --> 00:42:35,719
In this situation, surgery is necessary.

750
00:42:35,719 --> 00:42:37,320
That's just the surgeons' bias!

751
00:42:37,559 --> 00:42:38,880
During the consultation that day...

752
00:42:39,039 --> 00:42:39,880
Excuse us.

753
00:42:39,960 --> 00:42:40,880
didn't Internal Medicine say

754
00:42:40,880 --> 00:42:41,559
she could avoid surgery?

755
00:42:41,559 --> 00:42:42,760
Keep your voice down.

756
00:42:42,760 --> 00:42:43,199
Sorry.

757
00:42:43,199 --> 00:42:44,400
There are other people around.

758
00:42:44,719 --> 00:42:46,920
None of us know which method is safest,

759
00:42:46,920 --> 00:42:48,320
but we can calculate the odds.

760
00:42:48,599 --> 00:42:50,760
You can't risk Mom's life over your bias.

761
00:42:51,079 --> 00:42:52,480
I don't understand your fancy talk.

762
00:42:53,440 --> 00:42:54,519
I just don't agree.

763
00:42:54,599 --> 00:42:55,519
I'm her daughter.

764
00:42:55,519 --> 00:42:57,000
I can take responsibility for my decision.

765
00:42:57,000 --> 00:42:57,679
Can you?

766
00:42:57,679 --> 00:42:58,920
I'm her husband.

767
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:01,280
And I'm still your father!

768
00:43:08,119 --> 00:43:08,719
Hello, everyone.

769
00:43:08,719 --> 00:43:10,159
I'm actress Zhou Yiran,

770
00:43:10,440 --> 00:43:12,159
inviting you to watch the drama series

771
00:43:12,159 --> 00:43:12,880
"Confrontation."

772
00:43:14,320 --> 00:43:16,119
Newspaper front page, headline news.

773
00:43:16,119 --> 00:43:17,639
The base numbers have been deciphered.

774
00:43:17,639 --> 00:43:19,280
Most of the ciphers are identical.

775
00:43:20,199 --> 00:43:21,199
Notice:

776
00:43:21,199 --> 00:43:22,840
Two people are released today.

777
00:43:22,840 --> 00:43:24,239
Cao Liaoping, get ready first.

778
00:43:24,239 --> 00:43:25,840
Atoning through service, in my book,

779
00:43:25,840 --> 00:43:27,360
has never been just an empty slogan.

780
00:43:27,360 --> 00:43:29,480
Everything is digital now.

781
00:43:29,480 --> 00:43:30,800
No one uses film anymore.

782
00:43:30,800 --> 00:43:32,119
What will you store it in?

783
00:43:32,119 --> 00:43:33,280
Given time,

784
00:43:33,280 --> 00:43:36,639
I might steer the cross-strait intelligence tides.

785
00:43:36,639 --> 00:43:37,360
Wanna bet?
